    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n11 Upper Dargle Road is a charming one-bedroom townhouse offering a fantastic opportunity to create a truly special home in a well-established and convenient Bray location.\n\nAlthough in need a full renovation the property has been Vacant for approximately five years and now requiring complete renovation, the property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the property and purchaser meeting the relevant eligibility criteria and approval. For those looking for a renovation project, No. 11 offers an exciting blank canvas with plenty of original character and potential.\n\nThe accommodation is arranged over two floors and comprises an entrance hallway with staircase, a cosy living room featuring an original open fireplace, a compact kitchen and wetroom. Upstairs, there is a generous bedroom with a second original fireplace, another lovely reminder of the character of this traditional home.\nOne of the property's most appealing features is the private tiered rear garden. Elevated above the surrounding area, it enjoys wonderful views towards Bray Head and the church steeples of Bray. With some thoughtful landscaping, this could become a beautiful and peaceful outdoor retreat an ideal spot to relax and enjoy a summer evening.\n\nThe property offers excellent scope for refurbishment and possible extension. Architect's drawings are available illustrating how the house could potentially be transformed and extended, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nWhile the house requires complete renovation, it represents a wonderful opportunity for a first-time buyer, investor or downsizer to create a home to their own taste while retaining its original charm.\n\nUpper Dargle Road is an established residential area with excellent neighbours and a wonderful sense of community. The location is exceptionally convenient, with People's Park just around the corner and Bray town centre, Castle Street Shopping Centre, shops, cafés, supermarkets, schools and sporting facilities all within easy reach.\nBray's renowned Seafront and Promenade are also easily accessible, offering everything from a relaxed stroll by the sea to the famous Bray Head walk, along with the many cafés, restaurants and pubs for which the town is so well known.\n\nFor commuters, Bray DART station is approximately 1.5km away, while the N11/M50 corridor is easily accessible. Numerous bus services operate nearby, providing excellent connectivity to Dublin and the surrounding areas.\n\nKey Features\n\n• Charming one-bedroom townhouse full of character\n\n• Vacant for approximately five years\n\n• Potential to qualify for the Vacant Property \nRefurbishment Grant, subject to eligibility and approval\n\n• Complete renovation project with excellent potential\n\n• Original open fireplace in living room and original \nfireplace in bedroom\n\n• Private tiered rear garden with wonderful elevated views\n\n• Beautiful outlook towards Bray Head and Bray's church steeples\n\n• On-street parking only.\n\n• Architect's drawings available showing potential renovation and extension options\n\n• Excellent opportunity for a first-time buyer, investor or downsizer\n\n• Superb location close to People's Park, Bray town centre, seafront, DART and excellent transport links"
      },
